      "title": "We are implementing Step 2 of the Agentic SDLC project. IMPORTANT: Keep the project simple. The .sdlc/ directory has been intentionally removed. Do NOT recreate it. Do NOT create: - .sdlc/ - state.json - state-manager.js - validate-artifacts.js - validate-traceability.js - custom SDLC framework - GitHub Actions - PR creation scripts yet For this step ONLY, create the SDLC Orchestrator Agent, its Prompt, and its Skill. ================================================== PROJECT ================================================== Project: todo-agentic-sdlc-claude Purpose: Demonstrate an end-to-end Agentic SDLC using Claude Code. The application itself is intentionally simple: - Add Todo - Edit Todo - Delete Todo Do not expand the application scope. ================================================== EXISTING SDLC AGENTS ================================================== The following agents already exist and must be reused: .claude/agents/ requirements.agent.md architecture.agent.md design-review.agent.md implementation-planning.agent.md implementation.agent.md code-review.agent.md verification.agent.md pr-preparation.agent.md Do NOT recreate or replace these agents. ================================================== CREATE ORCHESTRATOR AGENT ================================================== Create: .claude/agents/sdlc-orchestrator.agent.md The orchestrator is responsible for coordinating the complete SDLC. It must NOT implement application code itself. It must invoke/use the existing phase agents in the correct order. ================================================== SDLC ORDER ================================================== The orchestrator must coordinate: 1. Requirements Agent 2. HITL Gate #1 3. Architecture Agent 4. Design Review Agent 5. HITL Gate #2 6. Implementation Planning Agent 7. Implementation Agent 8. Code Review Agent 9. Verification Agent 10. HITL Gate #3 11. PR Preparation Agent 12. PR authorization 13. Later, Claude Code hook will handle GitHub PR creation. For THIS step, do not implement the hook. ================================================== SOURCE OF TRUTH ================================================== The source of truth is: docs/user-story.md The original user story comes from the Confluence page: Todo Application - User Story User Story: \"As a user, I want to manage my todo items so that I can keep track of the tasks I need to complete.\" Acceptance Criteria: AC-1 Add Todo Given the application is open, when the user enters a todo and selects Add, then the item is added to the todo list. AC-2 Edit Todo Given a todo exists, when the user selects Edit and updates it, then the todo displays the updated text. AC-3 Delete Todo Given a todo exists, when the user selects Delete, then the todo is removed. The orchestrator must ensure that agents use the approved artifacts and user story rather than inventing requirements. ================================================== PHASE RESPONSIBILITIES ================================================== Requirements Agent: Input: docs/user-story.md Output: requirements.md Architecture Agent: Input: requirements.md Output: architecture.md Design Review Agent: Input: requirements.md architecture.md Output: design-review.md Implementation Planning Agent: Input: requirements.md architecture.md design-review.md Output: impl-plan.md Implementation Agent: Input: requirements.md architecture.md design-review.md impl-plan.md Output: todo-app/ Code Review Agent: Input: requirements.md architecture.md impl-plan.md todo-app/ Output: code-review.md Verification Agent: Input: requirements.md architecture.md impl-plan.md todo-app/ code-review.md Output: verification.md PR Preparation Agent: Input: requirements.md architecture.md design-review.md impl-plan.md code-review.md verification.md todo-app/ Output: PR.md CHANGELOG.md ================================================== ORCHESTRATOR RULES ================================================== The orchestrator must: - execute phases in the correct order - use the existing agents - use their existing prompts - use their existing skills - verify expected artifacts before moving to the next phase - stop when a phase fails - report which phase failed - prevent skipping phases - respect HITL gates - never silently approve a human gate - never invent requirements - never expand the Todo application scope The orchestrator must NOT: - implement application functionality itself - rewrite approved artifacts unnecessarily - create a database - create a backend - create an API - create authentication - add localStorage - create React code - create unrelated Todo features - create a GitHub PR directly - merge a GitHub PR - force push - create GitHub Actions ================================================== HITL GATES ================================================== Define the three Human-in-the-Loop gates clearly. GATE #1 After: Requirements Agent → requirements.md The orchestrator must STOP. It must tell the human: \"Requirements phase is complete. Please review requirements.md and explicitly approve Gate #1 before Architecture begins.\" The orchestrator must NOT continue until explicit approval. Do not assume approval. ------------------------------------------ GATE #2 After: Architecture Agent → architecture.md AND Design Review Agent → design-review.md The orchestrator must STOP. It must tell the human: \"Architecture and Design Review are complete. Please review the artifacts and explicitly approve Gate #2 before Implementation Planning begins.\" Do not continue until explicit approval. ------------------------------------------ GATE #3 After: Verification Agent → verification.md Verification must PASS. Then the orchestrator must STOP. It must tell the human: \"Verification passed. Please explicitly approve Gate #3 before PR Preparation.\" Do not continue until explicit approval. ================================================== PR CREATION RESPONSIBILITY ================================================== The orchestrator must NOT execute: gh pr create The orchestrator must NOT execute: git push for PR automation. Later we will implement a Claude Code hook that performs: validation → feature branch → commit → push → gh pr create For this step, only define the boundary between the orchestrator and the future hook. ================================================== PR AUTHORIZATION ================================================== After all of these are satisfied: - Verification = PASS - Code Review = APPROVED - Gate #3 = explicitly APPROVED - PR Preparation = COMPLETE the orchestrator will later create: .claude/pr-authorized.json For now, define this as the expected final authorization mechanism. Do NOT implement the hook yet. Do NOT create the PR. ================================================== ORCHESTRATOR STATUS ================================================== The orchestrator should provide clear status such as: Current Phase: Requirements Status: IN PROGRESS or: Current Phase: Architecture Status: BLOCKED Reason: Waiting for HITL Gate #1 approval. Keep this simple. Do NOT create a separate state management framework. ================================================== FAILURE HANDLING ================================================== If an agent fails: STOP. Report: - phase - agent - expected artifact - failure reason Do not continue to later phases. If a required artifact is missing: STOP. Do not continue. ================================================== TRACEABILITY ================================================== The orchestrator must preserve this relationship: Confluence User Story ↓ Acceptance Criteria ↓ Requirements ↓ Architecture ↓ Design Review ↓ Implementation Plan ↓ Implementation ↓ Code Review ↓ Verification ↓ PR Preparation ↓ GitHub PR Requirements mapping: AC-1 → FR-001 → Add Todo AC-2 → FR-002 → Edit Todo AC-3 → FR-003 → Delete Todo ================================================== CREATE ORCHESTRATOR PROMPT ================================================== Create: .claude/prompts/sdlc-orchestrator.prompt.md The prompt must instruct Claude to execute the complete SDLC using the orchestrator. It must contain: - objective - source of truth - phase order - agent responsibilities - HITL gates - artifact expectations - failure handling - scope restrictions - PR automation boundary It must explicitly say: \"Do not create the GitHub PR directly. The final PR will be created by a Claude Code hook after explicit human approval.\" ================================================== CREATE ORCHESTRATOR SKILL ================================================== Create: .claude/skills/sdlc-orchestrator/ SKILL.md The skill must provide practical instructions for coordinating the SDLC. It should explain: - how to determine the current phase - which agent to use - required inputs - expected outputs - when to stop - when to request human approval - how to handle failures - how to preserve traceability - when the workflow reaches PR Preparation Keep it concise. Do NOT create a custom state-management system. ================================================== DO NOT MODIFY ================================================== Do not modify: todo-app/ requirements.md architecture.md design-review.md impl-plan.md code-review.md verification.md PR.md CHANGELOG.md unless absolutely necessary for the orchestrator integration. Do not modify existing agents, prompts, or skills. ================================================== DO NOT IMPLEMENT YET ================================================== Do NOT implement: - Claude Code hooks - .claude/settings.json - create-pr.ps1 - GitHub PR automation - git push - gh pr create - automatic merge - new test frameworks Those are later steps. ================================================== FINAL VALIDATION ================================================== After creating the three files, verify: .claude/ ├── agents/ │ └── sdlc-orchestrator.agent.md ├── prompts/ │ └── sdlc-orchestrator.prompt.md └── skills/ └── sdlc-orchestrator/ └── SKILL.md Verify that: - .sdlc/ does NOT exist - existing 8 agents remain - existing prompts remain - existing skills remain - no application code was changed - no GitHub PR was created - no Git push was performed Then report: 1. Files created 2. Orchestrator responsibilities 3. SDLC phase sequence 4. HITL gate design 5. What remains for the next step STOP after this step.",
